0.007147594355046749, 0.03551502153277397, 0.0049442993476986885, -0.031344495713710785, 0.03614453226327896, 0.02057720348238945, 0.020511629059910774, 0.02278049848973751, -0.01584274135529995, -0.012380420230329037, 0.034229762852191925, -0.014662404544651508, 0.03480681777000427, 0.020760811865329742, 0.022308362647891045, 0.004386918153613806, -0.008675474673509598, 0.024052638560533524, -0.008131207898259163], "index": 9, "object": "embedding"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7702, "total_tokens": 7702}}, "input": {"input": ["--- Record 2211 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management connector\nDescription: Identity Provisioning supports the SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management connector. You can configure it as source, target, and proxy system for your provisioning scenarios. See:    SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management (Source)      SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management (Target)      SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management (Proxy)    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-25\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: 26701\n\n--- Record 2212 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP Data Custodian - filter users by group display name\nDescription: The default write transformation is changed to support provisioning of users that are members of groups matching the set dc.group.prefix. This is possible by including a condition for filtering the users by group display name of their assigned groups. If the dc.group.prefix is set, only users assigned to groups that contain in their display name the set specific prefix will be provisioned. In case the property is not set, all users are provisioned to SAP Data Custodian, regardless of the group display name of their assigned groups.  See: SAP Data Custodian\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-25\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: 26701\n\n--- Record 2213 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP Datasphere connector\nDescription: Identity Provisioning supports the SAP Datasphere connector. You can configure it as source, target, and proxy system for your provisioning scenarios. See:    SAP Datasphere (Source)      SAP Datasphere (Target)      SAP Datasphere (Proxy)    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-25\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: 26701\n\n--- Record 2214 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP HANA Cloud, SAP HANA Database connector\nDescription: Identity Provisioning supports the SAP HANA Cloud, SAP HANA Database connector. You can configure it as source, target, and proxy system for your provisioning scenarios. See:    SAP HANA Cloud, SAP HANA Database (Source)      SAP HANA Cloud, SAP HANA Database (Target)      SAP HANA Cloud, SAP HANA Database (Proxy)    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-25\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: 26701\n\n--- Record 2215 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Skip create and delete operations of groups - removed\nDescription: Skipping the create and delete operations for groups has been removed from the write transformations of the SAP BTP XS Advanced UAA (Cloud Foundry) target system.  Previously, it was not possible to create or delete groups; it was expected that groups already exist in the target system, allowing Identity Provisioning to only update their members. Now, creating, updating, and deleting groups follow the standard processes.  See: SAP BTP XS Advanced UAA (Cloud Foundry)\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-25\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: 26701\n\n--- Record 2216 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Support for OAuth certificate authentication\nDescription: SAP CPQ support OAuth certificate authentication.See: SAP CPQ\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-25\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: 26701\n\n--- Record 2217 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Create Additional Service Keys and Restrict Its Authorities\nDescription: You can now create additional service keys with predefined authorizations defined by specific scopes.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: 3.2\n\n--- Record 2218 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Provisioning - Create and Delete Decentralized Identity Verification Tenants\nDescription: You can create and delete a tenant using the Decentralized Identity Verification Provisioning API.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: 3.2\n\n--- Record 2219 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Condition and skip update - changed behavior\nDescription: The behavior of target transformations that contain a combination of condition and skip operations for updates has been changed.  Previously, the skip operation was evaluated before the condition. If users or groups have been updated in the source system, they", " 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: 3.2\n\n--- Record 2219 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Condition and skip update - changed behavior\nDescription: The behavior of target transformations that contain a combination of condition and skip operations for updates has been changed.  Previously, the skip operation was evaluated before the condition. If users or groups have been updated in the source system, they are marked as skipped in the logs, and Identity Provisioning does not proceed to evaluate the condition. As a result, users or groups that do not meet the condition are not deleted as they should be. After the change, the condition is evaluated first.  See: Transformation Expressions\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-25\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 2220 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Reset of SAP Master Data Integration - changed behavior\nDescription: Resetting the SAP Master Data Integration source system also resets the delta load marker.  Previously, the reset cleared the operational data without resetting the delta marker. This approach prevented the provisioning of old events in subsequent job runs. Now, the reset procedure for this system is consistent with that of the other supported source systems.  See: SAP Master Data Integration  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-09-25\nValid as Of: 2024-09-25\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 921 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Download all deleted entities for a provisioning job\nDescription: You can now download and view the details of all deleted entities by a provisioning job. To enable this, set the property ips.trace.deleted.entity to true.  For more information, see Manage Provisioning Job Logs and List of Properties.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-08\nValid as Of: 2025-05-08\nVersion: 27806\n\n--- Record 922 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Manage Corporate Identity Providers\nDescription: Tenant administrator can manage corporate identity providers in Identity Authentication via API. It offers endpoints for CRUD operations (GET, POST, PATCH, DELETE) over the corporate identity providers. See SAP Cloud Identity Services Corporate Identity Providers Directory.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-08\nValid as Of: 2025-05-08\nVersion: 27806\n\n--- Record 923 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Privacy Policy and Terms of Use\nDescription: The Identity Directory API of SAP Cloud Identity Services now returns the termsOfUse and privacyPolicy parameters. See Identity Directory API.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-08\nValid as Of: 2025-05-08\nVersion: 27806\n\n--- Record 924 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-08\nValid as Of: 2025-05-08\nVersion: 27806\n\n--- Record 925 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: REST API\nDescription: The Identity Directory API now supports new attribute externalName located in the group extension schema urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:sap:2.0:Group. The externalName attribute is unique within the application. See Identity Directory API.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-08\nValid as Of: 2025-05-08\nVersion: 27806\n\n--- Record 926 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition - schema support\nDescription: The default transformations of SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition are extended to support the urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:sap:2.0:User and urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:2.0:mapping schema.  See SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-08\nValid as Of: 2025-05-08\nVersion: 27806\n\n--- Record 927 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP ODM User Schema Support\nDescription: The default read and proxy read transformations in Identity Authentication and the Local Identity Directory support the urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:sap.odm:2.0:User schema. This custom SCIM schema extension is defined by SAP’s Organizational Data Model (ODM) and is used to enrich the standard SCIM User resource with SAP-specific attributes such as workAssignment, jobDetails, plant, and others.  See    Identity Authentication      Local Identity Directory    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-08\nValid as Of: 2025-05-08\nVersion: 27806\n\n--- Record 928 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAP Sales Cloud and SAP Service Cloud - new version\nDescription: A new connector version for SAP Sales Cloud and SAP Service Cloud  is introduced. It is applicable for SAP Sales Cloud Version 2 and SAP Service Cloud Version 2 and supports certificate-based authentication, patch operations, delta read of entities, cursor-based pagination and more.  See      SAP Sales Cloud and SAP Service Cloud (Source)      SAP Sales Cloud and SAP Service Cloud (Target)      SAP Sales Cloud and SAP Service Cloud (Proxy)    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-08\nValid as Of: 2025-05-08\nVersion: 27806\n\n--- Record 929 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Support for SAP extension schema for groups\nDescription: The default transformations of the following connectors support attributes from the SAP extension schema for groups, including application ID, type, and supported operations.  See:      SAP Central Business Configuration      SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition      SAP BTP ABAP environment      SAP Commerce Cloud      SAP Advanced Financial Closing    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 202", ",Neo\nTitle: Support for SAP extension schema for groups\nDescription: The default transformations of the following connectors support attributes from the SAP extension schema for groups, including application ID, type, and supported operations.  See:      SAP Central Business Configuration      SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition      SAP BTP ABAP environment      SAP Commerce Cloud      SAP Advanced Financial Closing    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-08\nValid as Of: 2025-05-08\nVersion: 27806\n\n--- Record 930 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition - schema support\nDescription: The default transformations of SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition are extended to support the urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:sap:2.0:User and urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:extension:2.0:mapping schema.  For more information, see SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-08\nValid as Of: 2025-05-08\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3181 ---\nComponent: Commercial Models\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: New commercial model available - SAP BTP Enterprise Agreement (SAP BTPEA)\nDescription: The new consumption-based commercial model, SAP BTP Enterprise Agreement (SAP BTPEA), is now available.  SAP BTPEA is an evolution of the existing Cloud Platform Enterprise Agreement (CPEA) commercial model. It offers high flexibility and the ability to keep a fixed spend, whereby you're billed only for actual cloud service consumption. SAP BTPEA comes with an updated and streamlined scope of services which you can activate and deactivate at any time. It introduces an adjusted deprecation policy, and opens the commercial model to additional SAP applications. See:    What Is the Consumption-Based Commercial Model?      SAP Discovery Center Service Catalog    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-10\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3182 ---\nComponent: Custom Domain Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Support for TLS 1.3\nDescription: You now have the option to enable TLS 1.3 for your SSL host with the --supported-protocols parameter of the set-ssl-host command.   See set-ssl-host.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-04\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3183 ---\nComponent: Extensions\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Enable Data Ingestion for Industry Cloud Solutions\nDescription: You can now set up on SAP BTP systems that support data ingestion and are part of the industry cloud solutions published by SAP. To do that, you need to include them in a formation of type Data Ingestion for Industry Cloud Solutions. When you create a new formation of type Data Ingestion for Industry Cloud Solutions, a system of type Data Ingestion for Industry Cloud Solutions is automatically added to the Systems list and included in this formation.  See Automating Integrations with Data Ingestion for Industry Cloud Solutions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-04\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3184 ---\nComponent: Extensions\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Enable System Landscape for SAP Build\nDescription: You can now discover and consume the APIs exposed by the SAP S/4HANA Cloud systems in your system landscape when you develop and extend applications on SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment, using SAP Build. To do this, first you need to enable connectivity between your system landscape in SAP BTP cockpit and SAP Build. The integration requires performing several configuration steps starting with configuration on a global account level, and then, configuration on a subaccount level.  See Setting Up System Landscape for SAP Build.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-04\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3185 ---\nComponent: Monitoring Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: New Certificate Validity Metric\nDescription: There is a new Certificate Validity metric to help you monitor expiring certificates. By default, you see the client certificate with the earliest expiration, but you can customize the default setting. See Certificate Validity Metric.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-04\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3186 ---\nComponent: Monitoring Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Use of Comments for Documentation Feedback\nDescription: You can now add comments to provide feedback directly on SAP Help Portal for the SAP Monitoring Service documentation. See Giving Feedback on SAP Documentation and Creating Better Documentation Together: SAP Help Portal’s new approach to Collaboration and Feedback.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-04\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3187 ---\nComponent: Object Store\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Cross-consumption from Kyma on GCP\nDescription: Object Store Service can be cross-consumed from Kyma on GCP. Please refer Consumption in the Kyma Environment for more details.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-04\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3188 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New User Menu, Settings Dialog and About Dialog Design in SAP BTP Cockpit\nDescription: We've added a new User Menu, Settings dialog, and About dialog design in SAP BTP cockpit. Additionally, you will now find the content for the User Information dialog in the Settings dialog. The Help and Support page as well as the Useful Links are now removed from the side navigation bar, and added to the new User Menu.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-04\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3189 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP", " now find the content for the User Information dialog in the Settings dialog. The Help and Support page as well as the Useful Links are now removed from the side navigation bar, and added to the new User Menu.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-04\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3189 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 39.3.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 39.0.0 to 39.3.0.      https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v39.3.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v39.2.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v39.1.0    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-04\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3190 ---\nComponent: SAP HANA Service\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Revision 2.00.059.12\nDescription: You can now update to SAP HANA revision 2.00.059.12. See 3409433 - SAP HANA 2 SPS05 Revision 059.12.    Note  If you are still on SAP HANA 1.0, upgrade to the latest version of SAP HANA 2.0 as SAP HANA 1.0 has reached the end of mainstream maintenance in June 2021. See 2946614 - End-of-Maintenance of SAP HANA 1.0 in the SAP BTP, Neo Environment.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-04\nValid as Of: 2024-04-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 761 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Sorting Space Members, Space Quotas, Security Groups\nDescription: On the Space Members page in the cockpit, you can now sort space members by update date or e-mail, and also in ascending or descending order.  On the Space Quotas page, you can sort space quotas by update date or space quota name, and also in ascending or descending order.  On the Security Groups page, you can sort security groups by update date or security group name, and also in ascending or descending order.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-29\nValid as Of: 2025-05-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 762 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 49.0.0\nDescription: Cloud Foundry has been updated from 48.9.0 to 49.0.0.  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v49.0.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v48.11.0  https://github.com/cloudfoundry/cf-deployment/releases/tag/v48.10.0  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-16\nValid as Of: 2025-05-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 763 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Multiple Subscriptions to SAP Build Work Zone Editions\nDescription: It’s now possible to subscribe to multiple SAP Build Work Zone editions in a given SAP BTP subaccount. (This reverts the previous announcement about multiple subscriptions not being supported , published on 23.1.2025).  Remaining restriction - you can’t subscribe to SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition and SAP SuccessFactors Work Zone in the same subaccount. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-29\nValid as Of: 2025-05-29\nVersion: 2505A\n\n--- Record 764 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Preview SAPUI5 Latest Version\nDescription: Administrators can enable the new site setting, Preview SAPUI5 Latest Version  on selected non-productive sites and test the latest SAPUI5 version for a period of two weeks.  After two weeks, the version becomes the default SAPUI5 version and is consumed automatically by all sites.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-29\nValid as Of: 2025-05-29\nVersion: 2505A\n\n--- Record 765 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Multiple Subscription to SAP Build Work Zone Editions\nDescription: It’s now possible to subscribe to multiple SAP Build Work Zone editions in a given SAP BTP subaccount. (This reverts the previous announcement about multiple subscription not being supported , published on 23.1.2025).  Remaining restriction - you can’t subscribe to SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition and SAP SuccessFactors Work Zone in the same subaccount. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-29\nValid as Of: 2025-05-29\nVersion: 2505A\n\n--- Record 766 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Preview SAPUI5 Latest Version\nDescription:  Administrators can enable the new site setting Preview SAPUI5 Latest Version on selected non-productive sites and test the latest SAPUI5 version for a period of two weeks.   After two weeks, the latest version becomes the default SAPUI5 version and is consumed automatically by all sites.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-29\nValid as Of: 2025-05-29\nVersion: 2505A\n\n--- Record 767 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2025.11\nDescription: New and changed features are available for administration, data cataloging, data integration, data modeling, and space management.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2025.11. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-29\nValid as Of: 2025-05-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 768 ---\nComponent: SAP Java Buildpack\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Version 2.30.0\nDescription: SAP Java Buildpack 2 has been updated from version 2.29.0 to 2.30.0. Updated components:       com.fasterxml.jackson is updated from version 2.18.3 to 2.19.0      com.sap.core.connectivity.jco is updated from version 3.4.9 to 5.0.1      commons-codec is updated from version 1.16.0 to 1.16.1      commons-io is updated from version 2.16.1", " updated from version 2.29.0 to 2.30.0. Updated components:       com.fasterxml.jackson is updated from version 2.18.3 to 2.19.0      com.sap.core.connectivity.jco is updated from version 3.4.9 to 5.0.1      commons-codec is updated from version 1.16.0 to 1.16.1      commons-io is updated from version 2.16.1 to 2.18.0    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-20\nValid as Of: 2025-05-29\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 769 ---\nComponent: Authorization and Trust Management Service\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Increased Priority of Security Recommendation BTP -UAA-0008 for Custom Identity Providers\nDescription: In security recommendation BTP-UAA-0008, we recommend using a custom identity provider in productive landscapes. We've raised the priority of this recommendation from Advanced to Critical and updated the description to highlight that you, as an administrator, have no control over credential and authentication policies or the user lifecycle of users in the default identity provider.  Action  In productive landscapes, configure the service to use SAP Cloud Identity Services as the custom identity provider.  Note  For SAP BTP, partner-managed edition, custom identity providers for platform users aren't supported.  For more information, see BTP-UAA-0008.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-28\nValid as Of: 2025-05-28\nVersion: 2505a\n\n--- Record 770 ---\nComponent: Java Server\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Tomcat version for Java Web Tomcat 10\nDescription: Java Web Tomcat 10 (runtime version 5.23) has been updated to Tomcat version 10.1.40.  See the Changelog and Security Fixes.  Recommended action: Update your applications to the latest runtime version. See Keeping Your Application Runtimes Up-to-date.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-28\nValid as Of: 2025-05-28\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3171 ---\nComponent: Integration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:  